      "writtenOn": "2026-06-26T19:12:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I can see, `SkIcoCodec` is not used directly in AOSP, at least a quick [code search](https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003dSkIcoCodec\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fgoogleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain) returns no caller (apart from Skia).\n\n[`ImageDecoder`](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/libs/hwui/jni/ImageDecoder.cpp;l\u003d117?q\u003dimagedecoder.cpp\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fgoogleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain), however, uses `SkCodec::MakeFromStream`, and I think it handles .ico files.\n\nSo I’m not sure if the factory option is possible here, WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "9277fd46_f9ff300d",
      "revId": "5d846b7f060558fd7a120d2f184e8f08e6c9d872",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
